1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,100
Jobs and Queue is the primary view while durable work runs.

2
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:09,625
Filter the status, expand the record and read timestamps, diagnostics,

3
00:00:09,862 --> 00:00:11,950
logs and the linked configuration.

4
00:00:12,325 --> 00:00:16,700
A verification failure can matter even when the subprocess returned

5
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:17,212
zero.

6
00:00:17,612 --> 00:00:20,700
Preserve terminal evidence before retention cleanup.

7
00:00:21,112 --> 00:00:24,850
Removing a queue record does not undo a target operation.

8
00:00:26,046 --> 00:00:30,971
Open Approvals and inspect the request, exact input, target and requester

9
00:00:30,983 --> 00:00:31,496
notes.

10
00:00:31,958 --> 00:00:35,358
Follow the required reviewer separation and expiry rules.

11
00:00:35,771 --> 00:00:38,233
Approve only the intended change;

12
00:00:38,708 --> 00:00:42,808
a deployment approval does not automatically approve later configuration.

13
00:00:43,221 --> 00:00:46,821
If the configuration changes, obtain its matching approval.

14
00:00:47,233 --> 00:00:51,096
Historical approval records support audit, but do not establish that

15
00:00:51,096 --> 00:00:53,558
the requested operation ran successfully.

16
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:58,492
Choose a repeatable action with a supported scheduled path, supply

17
00:00:58,504 --> 00:01:02,817
its reviewed input and enter the five-field U T C cron expression.

18
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:07,617
Test manually, then enable and verify an actual scheduled run.

19
00:01:08,029 --> 00:01:09,129
Pause for maintenance.

20
00:01:09,529 --> 00:01:13,979
Mandatory-approval workflows may be rejected by automation surfaces

21
00:01:14,092 --> 00:01:16,067
without an appropriate approval binding.

22
00:01:16,467 --> 00:01:19,254
Do not assume missed runs are replayed after downtime.

23
00:01:20,433 --> 00:01:25,571
Parallel Exec submits the same supported legacy workflow for multiple

24
00:01:25,571 --> 00:01:26,821
labelled site inputs.

25
00:01:27,208 --> 00:01:32,358
Check isolation of targets, credentials, addresses, images and services

26
00:01:32,358 --> 00:01:32,908
first.

27
00:01:33,308 --> 00:01:37,046
This screen is not proof that classic Foundation V M can run

28
00:01:37,183 --> 00:01:38,371
overlapping sessions.

29
00:01:38,771 --> 00:01:42,958
Use separately supported deployment paths and coordinate resource

30
00:01:42,958 --> 00:01:43,471
ownership.

31
00:01:43,871 --> 00:01:48,133
Inspect every site result because an aggregate success indicator can

32
00:01:48,133 --> 00:01:49,621
hide partial outcomes.

33
00:01:50,808 --> 00:01:55,233
A cancellation request or process interruption does not guarantee

34
00:01:55,433 --> 00:01:57,208
that an external operation stopped.

35
00:01:57,596 --> 00:02:01,508
Inspect Foundation or Prism and reconcile actual state.

36
00:02:01,908 --> 00:02:05,083
Keep successful steps and uncertainty recorded.

37
00:02:05,521 --> 00:02:10,033
For recovery, use its reconciliation and next-step linking controls.

38
00:02:10,433 --> 00:02:15,358
Never repeat destructive imaging or an uncertain password change simply

39
00:02:15,521 --> 00:02:17,796
to produce a cleaner execution history.
